Usage:
  nucleus openapi [flags]

Export the application's OpenAPI document: the one it derives from its routes and serves with WithOpenAPIDocument, read by booting it without listening (like routes). A project whose application serves no document and keeps a hand-written internal/contracts exports that contract, as before; --from picks the source explicitly.

Flags:
  -dir string
    	Directory of the application's main package, for --from app (default: the project root)
  -from string
    	Where the document comes from: app (boot the application and read the document it derives from its routes and serves), contracts (internal/contracts.NewDocument(), the hand-written contract alone), or auto (app, unless the application serves no document and the project has internal/contracts) (default "auto")
  -out string
    	Output path for the exported OpenAPI JSON document, or - for stdout (default "openapi.json")
  -project string
    	Project root that contains go.mod and internal/contracts (default ".")
  -timeout duration
    	How long the built application may take to print its document before it is killed (the build is not counted) (default 30s)

Examples:
  nucleus openapi --out openapi.json
  nucleus openapi --project ./svc --out -
  nucleus openapi --from contracts --out contract.json
